questions.a:
In order to register to vote, an individual must be:

1. A citizen of the United States;
2. A resident of the State of Missouri; and
3. 17 years and 6 months of age (must be 18 by Election Day).

If an individual meets these requirements, they are entitled to register to vote. To be entitled to vote, a person:

1. Must be registered to vote in the jurisdiction of the person's domicile prior to the election;
2. Cannot be imprisoned;
3. Cannot be on probation or parole after conviction of a felony pursuant to chapter 566 (https://revisor.mo.gov/main/OneChapter.aspx?chapter=566) or 573 (https://revisor.mo.gov/main/OneSection.aspx?section=573) or section 565.020 (https://revisor.mo.gov/main/OneSection.aspx?section=565.020), 565.021 (https://revisor.mo.gov/main/OneSection.aspx?section=565.021), 565.050 (https://revisor.mo.gov/main/OneSection.aspx?section=565.050), 565.052 (https://revisor.mo.gov/main/OneSection.aspx?section=565.052), 565.072 (https://revisor.mo.gov/main/OneSection.aspx?section=565.072), 565.079 (https://revisor.mo.gov/main/OneSection.aspx?section=565.079), 568.020 (https://revisor.mo.gov/main/OneSection.aspx?section=568.020), 568.045 (https://revisor.mo.gov/main/OneSection.aspx?section=568.045), or 569.160 (https://revisor.mo.gov/main/OneSection.aspx?section=569.160);
4. Cannot have been convicted of a felony or misdemeanor connected to voting; and
5. Cannot have been declared incapacitated.

